														<div data-panel="{&quot;clickOnActivate&quot;:&quot;firstChild&quot;}" role="button" class="forum_topic forum_topic_mini  unread">
								<div class="forum_topic_details">
									<div class="forum_topic_reply_count" title="1 reply">
										<img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/comment_quoteicon.png"> 1									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="forum_topic_name" title="From the demo, I want to like the game; however, compared to Punch-Out, the controls feel sluggish. Also the retro style is nice, but at times counter-productive (having a tutorial or hints for controller to learn the ropes would be nice). 

Pixel art is nice, but more stances/frames to make it more fluid would also add to at least a feeling of responsiveness. Currently the game a bit too slow.">
									<a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/3740090/discussions/0/573805391546437625/">
										First impressions									</a>
								</div>
							</div>
														<div data-panel="{&quot;clickOnActivate&quot;:&quot;firstChild&quot;}" role="button" class="forum_topic forum_topic_mini  unread">
								<div class="forum_topic_details">
									<div class="forum_topic_reply_count" title="13 replies">
										<img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/comment_quoteicon.png"> 13									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="forum_topic_name" title="The aging system feels far too aggressive. Once a boxer reaches the age of 26–27, their stats suddenly start declining at an unrealistic rate.

At 26–27, a professional boxer is still in their prime. There's no reason for an athlete to experience such a significant drop in performance simply because of aging. At that age, major stat reductions should only occur as a consequence of serious injuries or substantial damage sustained during fights.

I would suggest introducing a gradual decline in physical ">
									<a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/3740090/discussions/0/565923725076130462/">
										Boxer Aging System Is Too Aggressive – Stats Decline Too Early									</a>
								</div>
							</div>
														<div data-panel="{&quot;clickOnActivate&quot;:&quot;firstChild&quot;}" role="button" class="forum_topic forum_topic_mini  unread">
								<div class="forum_topic_details">
									<div class="forum_topic_reply_count" title="1 reply">
										<img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/comment_quoteicon.png"> 1									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="forum_topic_name" title="Can we have the prize money changed to  realistic figures, the early fights against low ranked fighters should be 5 to 15k the fights for the belts should be in the millions, this would give you that Championship feeling, then we could have trainer hire and gym rental more apartments cars horses which you can gamble on to spend your bucks on.
Awesome game though very addictive and reminded me of Barry McGuigans boxing on my old Amstrad, i even named one of the roster fighters &quot;Cannonball Corby&quot;.">
									<a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/3740090/discussions/0/573805391546390663/">
										Prize Money									</a>
								</div>
							</div>
														<div data-panel="{&quot;clickOnActivate&quot;:&quot;firstChild&quot;}" role="button" class="forum_topic forum_topic_mini  unread">
								<div class="forum_topic_details">
									<div class="forum_topic_reply_count" title="2 replies">
										<img src="https://community.akamai.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/comment_quoteicon.png"> 2									</div>
								</div>
								<div class="forum_topic_name" title="Not sure exactly what cheats the opponent is using, no padding in gloves, plaster of paris or whatever, but I savescummed a few times just to check it wasn't luck and he busts me open consistently with about 3-4 punches.  Whichever cheat he is using needs toning down, because his power stat sucks.

How fast the blood fills the screen also needs a look at, I'm forced to wipe it away every 3 seconds or so.  Weirder still, it's my lips he usually busts, which obviously wouldn't lead to any blood obscuring vis">
									<a href="https://steamcommunity.com/app/3740090/discussions/0/573805391546301448/">
										Think Cheating Opponents And Blood Both Need A Tinker									</a>
								</div>
							</div>
